---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Portrait from '../components/Portrait.astro';
import ClosingCta from '../components/ClosingCta.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Adam Malmborg | Project Pineapple"
  description="Running paid advertising since 2014, running businesses just as long. Why the practice exists and how it's run."
>
  <Header variant="full" />

  <section class="bio">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow bio__eyebrow">The short version</div>
      <h1>Adam Malmborg</h1>
      <div class="bio__text">
        <p class="lead">
          I've been running paid advertising since 2014, and running businesses just as long, and for most of that
          time I was doing both at once.
        </p>
        <p class="body body--long">
          I started in lead generation before it was called that, buying media for other people's businesses and
          learning what it costs to acquire a customer who actually pays. Then I started my own businesses and
          spent years on the other side of the table, deciding whether the marketing spend was worth it while also
          being responsible for payroll, pricing, hiring, and whether there was enough in the account at the end of
          the month.
        </p>
        <p class="body body--long">
          I've co-founded and operated businesses in custom retail, professional services, and the trades. Some
          worked well. Some taught me expensive lessons. All of them had marketing budgets I was personally
          accountable for.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="bio__portrait">
      <Portrait crop="feature" loading="eager" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--pine why">
    <h2 class="display-2">Why the practice exists</h2>
    <div class="why__text">
      <p class="body">
        At some point I noticed that every business I ran had the same problem with its marketing vendors. They
        reported on things the platform could see, and the platform couldn't see the sale. The reports looked
        fine. The revenue did whatever it was going to do. Nobody connected the two, because connecting them is
        genuinely hard work and nobody was being paid to do it.
      </p>
      <p class="pull why__pull">
        So that's the work. Figure out what a customer is worth, connect the sale back to where it came from, and
        rebuild the spending around what actually produced revenue. It isn't glamorous and it isn't fast. It is
        the thing that determines whether any of the rest of it worked.
      </p>
      <p class="body">
        Once that's in place, the numbers usually point at other things too. Leads that never got a call back,
        pricing nobody has revisited, card processing rates that were never negotiated. I've run businesses long
        enough to help with those, so I do.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="run">
    <h2 class="display-2">How I run this</h2>
    <div class="run__grid">
      <p class="run__p">
        I keep the client list short on purpose. Fewer clients means I'm in your account, not delegating it. You
        get me on the call, me in the reporting, and me making the recommendation. I don't run a team and I'm not
        building one.
      </p>
      <p class="run__p">
        I charge a flat monthly fee rather than a percentage of spend, so my recommendation about your budget
        isn't shaped by how it affects my invoice.
      </p>
      <p class="run__p">
        I'm based in Salt Lake City. Most of my clients aren't. It doesn't matter much for the work, though if
        you're local I'm happy to come by.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ClosingCta heading="Start with the assessment">
    Thirty minutes on where your growth is coming from, where it's leaking, and the two or three changes that would
    move the most. You keep the findings either way.
  </ClosingCta>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .bio {
    padding: var(--pad-hero) var(--gutter) var(--pad-major);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 5fr);
    gap: clamp(28px, 5.6vw, 96px);
    align-items: start;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .bio__eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: clamp(18px, 2vw, 26px);
  }
  .bio h1 {
    margin: 0 0 clamp(24px, 3vw, 40px);
    font: 400 clamp(44px, 6.6vw, 92px) / 1 var(--display);
    letter-spacing: -0.024em;
  }
  .bio__text {
    display: grid;
    gap: 22px;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .bio__portrait {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 460px;
    justify-self: end;
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .bio {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .bio__portrait {
      max-width: 300px;
      justify-self: start;
    }
  }

  .why {
    padding: var(--pad-major) var(--gutter);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
    gap: clamp(28px, 5.6vw, 104px);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .why h2 {
    max-width: 11ch;
  }
  .why__text {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(22px, 2.4vw, 30px);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .why .body {
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .why__pull {
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2vw, 26px);
    line-height: 1.42;
    color: var(--cream);
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .why {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .run {
    padding: var(--pad-major) var(--gutter);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .run__grid {
    margin-top: clamp(36px, 5vw, 72px);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 250px), 1fr));
    gap: clamp(28px, 3vw, 48px);
  }
  .run__p {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--pine);
    padding-top: clamp(18px, 2vw, 26px);
    font: 400 17px/1.68 var(--sans);
    color: var(--text-82);
  }
</style>
